ute"]},{"type":"p","text":"Strong for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Art museums"},{"text":"Galleries"},{"text":"Curatorial research"},{"text":"Art exhibitions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Path 4 — Museum Education"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA","Museum Education/Arts Education","Visitor & Public Programmes"]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Educational exhibitions"},{"text":"Workshops"},{"text":"Outreach"},{"text":"Community programmes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Government & Cultural Institution Route"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential employers include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government museums"},{"text":"Archaeological and heritage institutions"},{"text":"State museums"},{"text":"Cultural departments"},{"text":"Archives"},{"text":"Public galleries"},{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"Cultural centres"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Government positions are recruitment-specific, so eligibility, examination requirements and experience requirements should be checked for each current vacancy."},{"type":"h","text":"International Opportunities"},{"type":"p","text":"For international museum and heritage work, develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Museum studies"},{"text":"Heritage conservation"},{"text":"Exhibition practice"},{"text":"Art history"},{"text":"Cultural policy"},{"text":"Project management"},{"text":"Professional English"},{"text":"Digital heritage"}]},{"type":"p","text":"International experience can be built through:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Museum internships"},{"text":"Heritage research"},{"text":"Digital exhibitions"},{"text":"Cultural exchange projects"},{"text":"Academic research"},{"text":"International exhibition projects"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI & Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"p","text":"Technology is changing exhibitions from static displays into more interactive experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant technologies include:"},{"type":"h","text":"AI"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted visitor research"},{"text":"Automated metadata generation"},{"text":"Multilingual interpretation"},{"text":"Conversational museum guides"},{"text":"Personalised visitor experiences"},{"text":"Collection discovery"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AR/VR"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Virtual heritage reconstruction"},{"text":"Historical environments"},{"text":"Interactive object exploration"},{"text":"Immersive exhibitions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3D"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D scanning"},{"text":"Digital twins"},{"text":"Virtual collections"},{"text":"3D object documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"p","text":"Use visitor analytics to understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Visitor numbers"},{"text":"Dwell time"},{"text":"Popular exhibits"},{"text":"Programme attendance"},{"text":"Visitor demographics"},{"text":"Feedback"}]},{"type":"p","text":"AI should complement curatorial expertise rather than replace historical interpretation or provenance research."},{"type":"h","text":"Exhibition Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"A graduate should leave university with a portfolio containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Exhibition proposal"},{"text":"Curatorial concept"},{"text":"Gallery layout"},{"text":"Object list"},{"text":"Exhibition labels"},{"text":"Budget"},{"text":"Project timeline"},{"text":"Visitor journey"},{"text":"Digital exhibition"},{"text":"Exhibition evaluation report"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This can be more useful for an exhibition career than a certificate-heavy resume."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Technology Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Core"},{"type":"flow","items":["Excel","PowerPoint","Canva","Documentation Systems","Project Management"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Creative"},{"type":"flow","items":["Photoshop","Illustrator","InDesign"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Spatial"},{"type":"h","text":"QGIS + Basic 3D"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Heritage"},{"type":"flow","items":["3D scanning","Virtual Exhibitions","AR/VR fundamentals"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Management"},{"type":"flow","items":["Gantt charts","Budgeting","Procurement","Risk Management"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Position"],"rows":[[{"text":"BA"},{"text":"Museum/Exhibition Intern"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Exhibition Assistant / Museum Assistant"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Exhibition Coordinator"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior Exhibition Coordinator / Exhibition Manager"}],[{"text":"8–12 years"},{"text":"Exhibition Head / Museum Programme Manager"}],[{"text":"12+ years"},{"text":"Museum Director / Cultural Project Director / Exhibition Consultant"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Progression"},{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Museology + heritage + research foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Exhibition planning + interpretation + project management"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Exhibition production + internship + digital skills"}],[{"text":"Graduation"},{"text":"Complete exhibition portfolio + practical experience"}],[{"text":"0–2 Years"},{"text":"Exhibition/Museum Assistant"}],[{"text":"2–5 Years"},{"text":"Exhibition Coordinator"}],[{"text":"5–8 Years"},{"text":"Senior Coordinator / Exhibition Manager"}],[{"text":"8–12 Years"},{"text":"Exhibition Head / Programme Manager"}],[{"text":"12+ Years"},{"text":"Cultural Project Director / Consultant"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"flow","items":["Museology","Heritage Management","Exhibition Planning","Curatorial Research","Collections Documentation","Interpretation","Project Management","Budgeting","Vendor Coordination","Visitor Experience","Digital Exhibitions","Graphic Design","Accessibility","AR/VR","Cultural Communication"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"For this degree, the strongest career positioning is Exhibition Coordinator with combined curatorial, project-management and digital-exhibition capabilities. The degree provides the cultural and heritage foundation, while internships and hands-on exhibition projects provide the operational experience employers need. For long-term progression, adding a master's in Museology, Heritage Management, Museum Studies, Art History or a related field can strengthen access to specialist and managerial positions. The strongest future-oriented profile combines museum expertise + exhibition production + visitor experience + digital heritage technologies."}]}]}